---- MODULE MCCommittedStart ----
(*
This module defines an alternative initial state for a multi-node reads model
by extending an existing base specification, MultiNodeReads. It is intended for
use with a model checker like TLC to explore behaviors starting from a state
where two transactions have already been committed.
*)

EXTENDS MultiNodeReads

(*
Define some concrete transaction and node values to populate the initial state.
It is assumed that these values are valid members of the CONSTANTS defined
in the MultiNodeReads module (e.g., Txns and Nodes).
*)
txn1 == [op |-> "write", key |-> "x", val |-> 10]
txn2 == [op |-> "write", key |-> "y", val |-> 20]
n1 == "n1"
n2 == "n2"

\* @Init: An alternative initial state predicate.
\*
\* This state initializes the system as if two transactions have already
\* been successfully proposed and committed across two nodes. The `ledger`,
\* `branches` (local ledgers for each node), and `history` variables
\* are pre-populated to reflect this committed state.
Init ==
    LET
        \* The sequence of two committed transactions.
        committedLedger == <<txn1, txn2>>

        \* The history log reflecting the invocation and successful, committed
        \* completion of both transactions.
        committedHistory ==
            << [type |-> "invoke",    value |-> txn1],
               [type |-> "ok",        value |-> txn1],
               [type |-> "committed", value |-> txn1],
               [type |-> "invoke",    value |-> txn2],
               [type |-> "ok",        value |-> txn2],
               [type |-> "committed", value |-> txn2] >>
    IN
    /\ ledger = committedLedger
    /\ branches = [n \in {n1, n2} |-> committedLedger]
    /\ history = committedHistory
    \* This predicate only constrains the variables `ledger`, `branches`, and
    \* `history`. Any other variables declared in the MultiNodeReads module
    \* are assumed to be unconstrained by this predicate and may take any
    \* initial values permitted by their type invariants.

\* @Next: The next-state action for the system.
\*
\* We use the next-state action directly from the base module that this
\* specification extends.
Next == MCNextMultiNodeReadsAction

\* @Spec: The main temporal specification for the model checker.
\*
\* The specification states that the system starts in the alternative `Init`
\* state and subsequent states are generated by the `Next` action (or a
\* stuttering step where the state does not change). The `vars` tuple is
\* assumed to be defined in the MultiNodeReads module.
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars

=============================================================================